    description: "Phase 2 of WI-zimum (Phase 1 merged PR #2948, covered Go/Rust/Java/C#/Scala/Kotlin/Groovy via the modifier-based is_exported_from_modifiers helper). Phase 2 covers languages whose export semantics do not flow through modifiers: (1) Python module-level __all__ names and the leading-underscore convention, implemented in py.py at symbol extraction time; (2) TypeScript/JavaScript top-level export_statement nodes in js_ts.py, extending the existing Next.js handler export parser to set Symbol.is_exported. Out of scope: Rust pub-use re-export chains, TS barrel index files, Python from-X-import-Y re-exports. Validation: re-run WI-tubot prospector on airflow (Python) and apollo-server (TS), expect dead% to drop meaningfully from the 70-85% baseline."  # b43b
